; A MAP'S LENGTH IS |dom m| (maps.md §1).
; inputs: 0 1 5
; expect: 0 1 5
;
; `len` is one construct with one meaning -- the cardinality of the index set --
; at a different index set. Every table has one, so this is not a special case.
;
; It was wrong on THREE of the four targets and in three different ways, which
; is the argument for this suite in one line:
;
;   Go        len(m)                   correct already
;   JavaScript `{}.length`             SILENT: undefined
;   Java       `.length` on a Map      a compile error -- javac refused it
;   windows    the buffer's length     SILENT: 3 words a slot, so 48 for 5
;
; A host with types refused what the host without them printed. Neither
; silent answer could be caught by reading the emitted code for one target.
;
; On windows this needs binder tracking rather than a shape: after lowering, a
; map IS an array buffer, so `(len m)` and `(len a)` are the same term meaning
; different things. The identification happens while `build-map` is still
; visible, which is the only place the type exists.
(def run (fn (n)
  (let (build-map 8 (fn (m)
         (loop ((m m) (i 0))
           (@ge i n)  m
           else       (again (insert m i 1) (@add i 1)))))
    (fn (m) (len m)))))
